    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12048" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curto</span></b> , āvi, ātum, 1,
			v. a.
		curtus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to shorten, diminish</i> (not ante-Aug., and very
			rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 7,
					9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radices,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Feb. 10, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to diminish</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					6, 34</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Quantulum enim summae curtabit quisque dierum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 3, 124</span></i>
			.</div>
